export let structuredData = {
  "contents": [{
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "The early mistake of Fumadocs was Fumadocs CLI being too late and not getting enough mentions on docs."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "To push the CLI approach further like the recent Shadcn CLI support, there's changes we have to made.\nEarly adopters will face problems if their customisations went beyond what our abstraction can mitigate."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "For example: A small CSS change can still breaks hacky CSS customisations, we can only ensure backward compatibility for the ones scoped by CSS selectors, or exposed options:"
  }, {
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "For CLI to work better, we need layout components to be entirely independent for modularization. A ideal state is that:"
  }, {
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "Normal users can use exposed options, enjoying UI iterations from upstream."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "Advanced customisations can use Fumadocs CLI, avoiding upstream changes."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-mistake",
    "content": "Same as the solution described in this post about UI Customisation."
  }, {
    "heading": "a-good-example",
    "content": "For lighter customisations like nuqs did, a PR to migrate from old versions #1056 can reduce code on user land and migration is simple."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-problems",
    "content": "When your hacks is heavier, migration is much harder combined with the tech debt of your codebase."
  }, {
    "heading": "the-problems",
    "content": "Some problems I observed:"
  }, {
    "heading": "page-tree-api-being-neglected",
    "content": "Page tree is actually a crucial idea of Fumadocs, unifying all navigation & linking of docs."
  }, {
    "heading": "page-tree-api-being-neglected",
    "content": "Even in the early days, it's already a robust API supporting features like Root Folder (since v12):"
  }, {
    "heading": "page-tree-api-being-neglected",
    "content": "Some projects didn't rely on our file-based routing nor page tree API, which resulted in a lot of hacks around sidebar & loader()."
  }, {
    "heading": "page-tree-api-being-neglected",
    "content": "Its idea is simple:"
  }, {
    "heading": "page-tree-api-being-neglected",
    "content": "Using it properly can already reduce a massive amount of work, we have a specs for Page Tree for hardcoded page trees."
  }, {
    "heading": "css-variables-being-neglected",
    "content": "Fumadocs is using CSS variables for all colors since the beginning, the naming is identical to Shadcn UI which makes customisation easy."
  }, {
    "heading": "css-variables-being-neglected",
    "content": "But I noticed some are overriding the Tailwind CSS classes rather than colors, like:"
  }, {
    "heading": "css-variables-being-neglected",
    "content": "In fact we always support a simpler way:"
  }, {
    "heading": "css-variables-being-neglected",
    "content": "Now we also have a Shadcn UI preset to reuse your colors from main app."
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "I think the CLI approach is correct, it'll be the primary way for advanced customisation."
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "My future plans:"
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "Continue improving Fumadocs CLI: adding install-time optimization to remove unused files according to your options (e.g. use existing sidebar component instead of installing one)."
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "A better versioning policy: Reduce abstraction for mitigating upstream changes, instead version the components directly (e.g. creating a new fumadocs-ui/layouts/v2/page instead of a major UI change)."
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "Add Fumadocs-native cloud features: More official integrations like monitoring/analytics feature designed for Fumadocs."
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "My biggest goal is to build my own dev team or startup, I realized my time is too limited to build the excellent software in my imaginary.\nThere's rough edges that I never found time to polish, and too many things to do - even if AI has handled the basic work."
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "That's all I want to say :)"
  }, {
    "heading": "early-reflections",
    "content": "Welcome for questions (via DM/GitHub), I'm happy to improve rough edges whenever I have time."
  }],
  "headings": [{
    "id": "a-mistake",
    "content": "A Mistake"
